---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/main.astro";
import Header from "@/components/header.astro";
import { ConnectionAttemptDelayTest } from "@/components/tests/connection-attempt-delay-test.tsx";
---

<PageLayout title="HE CAD Test | Happy Eyeballs Webtester">
  <Header
    titleLine1="Happy Eyeballs"
    titleLine2="Connection Attempt Delay Test"
  >
    <p>
      We set up a server with as many unique IPv4 and IPv6 addresses as measured
      delays. Each delay has a corresponding IPv4 and IPv6 address bound to all
      subdomains of a delay-specific domain name. By using tc netem, we delay
      the traffic for the IPv6 address by the configured number of milliseconds.
      This enables us to test how browsers deploy Happy Eyeballs.
    </p>
    <p>
      We randomize domains to prevent caching effects on the browser's side. The
      measurement without randomization shows whether the browser caches or uses
      performance measurements to select IP versions. The web server only offers
      HTTP/1.1 to prevent connection reuse between tests.
    </p>
    <p>
      Please note that the connection attempt trace for this test is currently
      unreliable, as correlation requires an SNI to be present.
    </p>
  </Header>

  <ConnectionAttemptDelayTest client:load />
</PageLayout>
